==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*noga}}, from {{inh|bg|ine-bsl-pro|*nagā́ˀ}}, from {{inh|bg|ine-pro|*h₃nṓgʰs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|нога́}}

===Noun===
{{bg-noun|нога́|f}}

# {{lb|bg|dated|dialectal}} [[foot]]
#: {{syn|bg|ходи́ло|стъпа́ло}}
# {{lb|bg|dated|dialectal}} [[leg]]
#: {{syn|bg|крак|q1=regular term}}

====Usage notes====
In modern Bulgarian, the singular of {{l|bg|нога́}} is mostly obsolete. Only the dual {{l|bg|нозе́}} is being used, specifically in the sense [[feet]] {{gloss|the immovable part of the lower limb}}. The sense [[leg]] is nowadays conveyed by {{l|bg|крак}} (originally: [[spanning]], [[striding]] [[limb]]).

====Declension====
{{bg-ndecl|нога́</pl:нозе́:ноги́[r]:нози́[r]>}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|bg|подно́жие||foot of elvation}}, {{l|bg|подно́жка||foothold}}
* {{l|bg|но́кът||nail}}

===References===
* {{R:bg:RBE}}
* {{R:bg:RBE2}}

